NAME
       fsfreeze - pause or resume writes to a mounted file system

SYNOPSIS
       fsfreeze -f MOUNTPOINT
       fsfreeze -u MOUNTPOINT

DESCRIPTION
       fsfreeze -f writes everything waiting in memory to the file system and
       then holds all new writes, so that a storage snapshot taken now is
       consistent. fsfreeze -u lets writes continue. Programs that write
       while it is frozen simply wait. Run it as root, and never on /.

OPTIONS
       -f, --freeze
              Freeze the file system.

       -u, --unfreeze
              Thaw it again.

EXAMPLES
           fsfreeze -f /data
           fsfreeze -u /data

SEE ALSO
       lvcreate(8), mount(8)
